      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A new rapid and sensitive method for measurement of apolipoprotein B (Apo B) in plasma has been developed. This method, based on a Competitive Enzyme-Linked Immunoassay (CELIA), has been used to study the association between the extent of coronary artery occlusion as measured by coronary arteriography and the levels of plasma Apo B. The correlation between Apo B levels and some other plasma lipids was also determined. Significant relationship was found between the extent of coronary artery occlusion and Apo B, as well as between Apo B and plasma total cholesterol and plasma triglyceride levels."},
